Cardamom Privacy Policy
Last updated: September 30, 2026
Cardamom is a card game app. It's built to keep what's yours on your phone.
What Cardamom collects
Nothing. Cardamom has no accounts of its own, no analytics, no ads, and no tracking. It doesn't send your information to the developer or to anyone else.
What stays on your phone
	•	House rules and settings you create are saved only on your device.
	•	Photos you choose for the wallpaper or card backs: Cardamom only receives the one photo you pick (it never sees the rest of your library). It saves a smaller copy on your device, and deletes it when you tap Reset.
	•	These are included in your device's normal backups, like any app's data.
Playing online
Online games use Apple's Game Center. Apple handles sign-in, invitations, and the connection between players, under Apple's Privacy Policy. Other players in your game see your Game Center name.
The cards you play and any Table Talk chat messages are sent only to the other players in that game. Chat messages are kept in memory only while the game is open. They are never saved and disappear when the game ends.
Children
Cardamom doesn't knowingly collect information from anyone, including children.
Changes
If this policy changes, the new version will be posted here with a new date.
